{
  "id": "sat-expoly",
  "chapterNumber": "4",
  "title": {
    "en": "Exponentials, Polynomials &amp; Rational Expressions",
    "ar": null
  },
  "chapterTag": {
    "variant": "category",
    "className": "sat-domain-tag",
    "emoji": "📌",
    "categoryPrefix": "Domain:",
    "category": "Advanced Math",
    "topics": [
      "Equivalent expressions",
      "Nonlinear functions",
      "Nonlinear equations (radical, rational)"
    ]
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Beyond quadratics: exponential growth and decay, exponent rules, and simplifying polynomial and rational expressions.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Exponents &amp; growth",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( a^{m}a^{n}=a^{m+n} \\) and \\( (a^{m})^{n}=a^{mn} \\). An exponential model \\( y=a\\cdot b^{x} \\) grows when \\( b&gt;1 \\) and decays when \\( 0&lt;b&lt;1 \\); \\( a \\) is the starting value.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "In \\( y=2\\cdot b^{x} \\), a base \\( b&gt;1 \\) grows while \\( b&lt;1 \\) decays. Slide \\( b \\) and watch the curve flip behaviour around \\( b=1 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Exponential model",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "satExpCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "An exponential curve y equals 2 times b to the x with adjustable base",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "satExpDataBtn",
          "panelId": "satExpDataPanel",
          "descId": "satExpDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "satExpDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points along the current exponential curve",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "y",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "satBase",
            "label": {
              "en": "Base <b>b =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 0.5,
            "max": 2,
            "value": 1.5,
            "step": 0.1,
            "valueDisplayId": "satBaseV",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Base b",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "satExpType",
            "label": {
              "en": "behaviour",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "—"
          },
          {
            "id": "satExpY1",
            "label": {
              "en": "value at x = 1",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "amber",
            "value": "—"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Each \\( +1 \\) in \\( x \\) multiplies \\( y \\) by \\( b \\); the start value \\( (0,2) \\) is amber.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Product",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a^{m}a^{n}=a^{m+n} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Power",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (a^{m})^{n}=a^{mn} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Exponential",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( y=a\\cdot b^{x} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Simplify",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "cancel common factors",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( 2^{x}=16 \\).</p>\\[ x=4. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Simplify \\( \\dfrac{6x^{2}}{2x} \\).</p>\\[ 3x. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Radical Equations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Isolate the radical, then square both sides. <strong>Always check</strong> your answers — squaring can introduce extraneous solutions that don't satisfy the original equation. Require the expression under the radical to be \\(\\geq0\\) (domain restriction).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.C — Radical equation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\(\\sqrt{3x+1}=4\\).</p><p>Square: \\(3x+1=16\\Rightarrow x=5\\). Check: \\(\\sqrt{16}=4\\). \\checkmark</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Rational Equations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Multiply through by the LCD to clear fractions. Identify <strong>domain restrictions</strong> (values making any denominator zero) before solving. Discard any solution that equals a restricted value.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Rational eq.",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Multiply by LCD; exclude denominator zeros",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Extraneous root",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Satisfies cleared eq. but not original",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Domain restriction",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Denom. \\(\\neq0\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "\\(\\sqrt{a^2}=|a|\\)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Not simply \\(a\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.D — Rational equation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\(\\dfrac{3}{x-1}+\\dfrac{1}{x+1}=\\dfrac{4}{x^{2}-1}\\). Note \\(x\\neq\\pm1\\).</p><p>Multiply by \\((x-1)(x+1)\\): \\(3(x+1)+(x-1)=4\\Rightarrow4x+2=4\\Rightarrow x=\\tfrac{1}{2}\\). \\checkmark</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "<strong>SAT-style:</strong> Solve \\(\\sqrt{2x-5}=x-4\\). How many valid solutions are there?",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Square: \\((x-4)^2=x^2-8x+16=2x-5\\Rightarrow x^2-10x+21=0\\Rightarrow(x-3)(x-7)=0\\).<br>Check \\(x=3\\): \\(\\sqrt{1}\\neq-1\\). Extraneous. Check \\(x=7\\): \\(\\sqrt{9}=3\\). \\checkmark<br><strong>One valid solution</strong>: \\(x=7\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
